<title>GERMANY: Workers fear job cuts at Mercedes trucks.</title>
<headline>Workers fear job cuts at Mercedes trucks.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 2,000 jobs are under threat from cost-cutting plans at the Mercedes-Benz AG truck assembly plant in Woerth near Stuttgart, the works council there said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Works council chairman Gerd Rheude said internal Mercedes documents estimated that putting the measures into effect would threaten some 2,000 of the 8,300 jobs there. Mercedes did not confirm the figures when contacted by Reuters.</p>
<p>Mercedes, which across its business is also facing fierce opposition from workers to sick pay cuts that came into effect at the start of this month, is seeking to make annual cuts of around a billion marks in its heavy trucks production activities.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
